      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Please do not administer aspirin or magnesium without explicit direction from a healthcare professional, especially while pregnant. These medications can be dangerous for you and your baby, and trying them based on a friend's experience is unsafe. Given your symptoms and your doctor's absence, call an on-call nurse line or a local OB/GYN advice line for immediate guidance. Your health and the baby's well-being are the most important things right now.",
      "source": "target",
